BE-300 2.4.18: split Hit_Writeback_Inv_D into writeback + invalidate.

VR4131 silicon has a documented D-cache bug: combined Hit_Writeback_Inv_D
(cache op 0x15) occasionally leaves a line in an inconsistent state
because the internal refill buffer is mishandled across the
writeback+invalidate sequence. The published workaround (see the linux4be
era patches/vr4131_cachebug_fix.patch and the 4.2.9 port's
patches/linux-4.2.9/be300/0003-linux-4.2.9-add-BE-300-runtime-fixes.patch)
is to issue Hit_Writeback_D (0x19) followed by Hit_Invalidate_D (0x11)
as two separate cache instructions.

This patch applies the split to the three Hit_Writeback_Inv_D sites in
include/asm-mips/r4kcache.h:

  * flush_dcache_line() — line-level flush.
  * blast_dcache16_page() — 16-byte-line page flush.
  * blast_dcache32_page() — 32-byte-line page flush.

All gated on CONFIG_VR4131_CACHE_FIX so non-BE-300 VR41xx targets are
unaffected. CONFIG_VR4131_CACHE_FIX=y is already in config_be300 (it
also picks pg-vr4131.o over pg-r4k.o in arch/mips/mm/Makefile).

The emulator does not simulate the D-cache and therefore does not
observe the bug; the test environment can't confirm the fix works on
real silicon, only that the kernel still boots clean with the split
in place. Required for any real-HW bring-up attempt — without it, the
2.4.18 kernel hangs at "Calibrating delay loop..." just like the same
bug observed on 4.2.9 (see CLAUDE.md "VR4131 cache bug").

--- a/include/asm-mips/r4kcache.h
+++ b/include/asm-mips/r4kcache.h
@@ -65,15 +65,38 @@
 
 static inline void flush_dcache_line(unsigned long addr)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_VR4131_CACHE_FIX
+	/*
+	 * VR4131 D-cache bug: combined Hit_Writeback_Inv_D (op 0x15)
+	 * occasionally leaves a line in an inconsistent state because the
+	 * internal refill buffer is mishandled. Issue separate
+	 * Hit_Writeback_D (op 0x19) + Hit_Invalidate_D (op 0x11). See
+	 * patches/vr4131_cachebug_fix.patch and the 4.2.9 port's
+	 * patches/linux-4.2.9/be300/0003 for the same split applied to
+	 * later kernels.
+	 */
 	__asm__ __volatile__(
 		".set noreorder\n\t"
 		".set mips3\n\t"
 		"cache %1, (%0)\n\t"
+		"cache %2, (%0)\n\t"
 		".set mips0\n\t"
 		".set reorder"
 		:
 		: "r" (addr),
+		  "i" (Hit_Writeback_D),
+		  "i" (Hit_Invalidate_D));
+#else
+	__asm__ __volatile__(
+		".set noreorder\n\t"
+		".set mips3\n\t"
+		"cache %1, (%0)\n\t"
+		".set mips0\n\t"
+		".set reorder"
+		:
+		: "r" (addr),
 		  "i" (Hit_Writeback_Inv_D));
+#endif
 }
 
 static inline void invalidate_dcache_line(unsigned long addr)
@@ -228,7 +251,13 @@
 	unsigned long end = (start + PAGE_SIZE);
 
 	while(start < end) {
+#ifdef CONFIG_VR4131_CACHE_FIX
+		/* VR4131 D-cache bug: split into writeback then invalidate. */
+		cache16_unroll32(start,Hit_Writeback_D);
+		cache16_unroll32(start,Hit_Invalidate_D);
+#else
 		cache16_unroll32(start,Hit_Writeback_Inv_D);
+#endif
 		start += 0x200;
 	}
 }
@@ -413,7 +442,13 @@
 
 	__asm__ __volatile__("nop;nop;nop;nop");
 	while(start < end) {
+#ifdef CONFIG_VR4131_CACHE_FIX
+		/* VR4131 D-cache bug: split into writeback then invalidate. */
+		cache32_unroll32(start,Hit_Writeback_D);
+		cache32_unroll32(start,Hit_Invalidate_D);
+#else
 		cache32_unroll32(start,Hit_Writeback_Inv_D);
+#endif
 		start += 0x400;
 	}
 }
